From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:16:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wallet(v2): sign chain-bound keyhash messages with compact
 ECDSA

Keep the existing signmessage/verifymessage RPC names and recoverable 65-byte Base64 envelope. Bind Lotus application signatures to exact message bytes and ChainID, resolve native BLAKE3(x-only) keyhashes in both key managers, reject noncanonical/high-S/native-header proofs, and retain the unchanged eCash primitives as byte-for-byte controls. Native transaction signatures remain BIP340. Add independent hashlib/RFC6979/pure-Python secp vectors, watch-only/encryption/restart coverage, and synchronize the canonical provisional specification.
